---
import Plain from '../layouts/Plain.astro';
import Ext from '../components/Ext.astro';
import H2 from '../components/H2.astro';
import SideH from '../components/SideH.astro';
import { link } from '../lib/ui';
import { experiences, contributions, archivedProjects, publications, photos, posts, WATCHLIST_MEDIA } from '../data';
const current = experiences.find((e) => /present/i.test(e.period));
const sortedPosts = [...posts].sort((a,b) => b.date.localeCompare(a.date));
const watching = WATCHLIST_MEDIA.filter((m) => m.category === 'current');
---
<Plain section="home">
  <header class="home-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Solutions architect · Sydney</p><h1>N.R.<br />Dhanawada</h1><p class="intro-line">Understand the problem.<br />Build what holds up.</p></header>
  <div class="home-copy">
    <p>I'm a solutions architect{current && <> at {current.company}</>}. I design the Salesforce side of government employment programs: the CRM architecture, the data pipelines, and the Lightning components over 500 staff use all day.</p>
    <p>Mostly, I find why something is broken and fix it properly instead of patching the symptom. It's what keeps things working on Monday morning.</p>
    <p><a href="/about" class={link}>Background, work & education →</a></p>
  </div>
  <H2>Selected work</H2>
  <article class="project-row"><span class="row-number">01</span><div><h3><a href="/projects/forcecalendar">forceCalendar</a></h3><p>A calendar engine and Web Components UI, built for the constraints of Salesforce. Pure JavaScript. Zero dependencies.</p><div class="row-meta">Open source · JavaScript · Web Components</div></div><a href="/projects/forcecalendar" class="row-arrow" aria-label="Read about forceCalendar">↗</a></article>
  <article class="project-row"><span class="row-number">02</span><div><h3><a href="/projects/servicecite">ServiceCite</a></h3><p>An independent reference for Australian employment services guidelines. Search, read, and get back to the source.</p><div class="row-meta">Reference tool · Australian employment services</div></div><a href="/projects/servicecite" class="row-arrow" aria-label="Read about ServiceCite">↗</a></article>
  <p class="mt-6"><a href="/projects" class={link}>All projects & upstream contributions →</a></p>
  <H2>Notes</H2><ul>{sortedPosts.map(post => <li class="note-row"><time datetime={post.date}>{post.date}</time><div><h3><a href={`/notes/${post.slug}`}>{post.title}</a></h3><p>{post.summary}</p></div></li>)}</ul>
  <H2>Elsewhere in the code</H2><ul class="space-y-4">{contributions.map(c => <li><Ext href={c.url}>{c.title}</Ext><span class="block row-meta">{c.org}/{c.repo}</span></li>)}</ul>
  <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-text-muted">Older, smaller things: {archivedProjects.map((p,i) => <Fragment><Ext href={p.links.github ?? p.links.live ?? p.links.firefox ?? '#'}>{p.title}</Ext>{i < archivedProjects.length-1 ? ', ' : '.'}</Fragment>)}</p>
  {publications[0] && <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-text-muted">And one undergraduate paper: <Ext href={publications[0].link}>{publications[0].title}</Ext>.</p>}
  <Fragment slot="sidebar">
    <figure><img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dyntcx472/image/upload/q_auto,f_auto,w_800/art002e000192_yso465" alt="Earth photographed from the Orion spacecraft window during Artemis II, April 2026" width="800" height="533" class="w-full h-auto" /><figcaption class="mt-3"><Ext href="https://www.nasa.gov/image-article/hello-world/">Hello, World</Ext><br />Earth from Orion, Artemis II, April 2026. NASA/Reid Wiseman. Not mine, but it's the best picture of where everyone's code runs.</figcaption></figure>
    <SideH>Away from the keyboard</SideH><p><a href="/art" class={link}>{photos.length} photographs →</a></p><p>Looking at light, streets, and the things in between.</p>
    <SideH>Currently watching</SideH><ul class="space-y-1">{watching.map(m => <li>{m.title}</li>)}</ul><p><a href="/tv" class={link}>The watchlist →</a></p>
    <SideH>Say hello</SideH><p><a href="mailto:nirmal@dhanawada.org" class={link}>nirmal@dhanawada.org</a></p><p><Ext href="https://github.com/thedhanawada">GitHub ↗</Ext></p><p>Code is easier to talk about than ideas, so if you have some, send it.</p>
  </Fragment>
</Plain>
